
.TH MYSTRCPY 1 "September 2026" "OS Assignment" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.br
.B char *mystrcpy(char *dest, const char *src);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrcpy
function copies the string pointed to by
.B src
into the character array pointed to by
.B dest.
The null terminating character is also copied.
The destination must have enough space to store the copied string.
